    <p><span style="color:#0066cc;"><strong>IMO</strong></span></p>

<p>The Hong Kong International Convention for the Safe and Environmentally Sound Recycling of Ships, 2009 (the Hong Kong Convention), was adopted at a diplomatic conference held in Hong Kong, China, from 11 to 15 May 2009, which was attended by delegates from 63 countries.&nbsp;Documents from the diplomatic conference are retrievable using the document symbol<strong> <a href="https://docs.imo.org/Category.aspx?cid=589" target="_blank">SR</a></strong><strong><a href="https://docs.imo.org/Category.aspx?cid=589" target="_blank">/CONF</a></strong> in the IMO document repository<strong> <a href="https://docs.imo.org/Category.aspx?cid=589" target="_blank">IMODOCS</a></strong> (registration required).&nbsp; Read more about IMO&#39;s work in Ship Recycling <em><strong><a href="https://www.imo.org/en/OurWork/Environment/Pages/Ship-Recycling.aspx" target="_blank">here</a></strong></em></p>

